Here's the performance analysis for `CaseTransformExtensions.cs`:

---

## Scan Execution Checklist

| Recipe | Hits |
|--------|------|
| `.ToLower()`/`.ToUpper()` without culture | 2 |
| `RegexOptions.Compiled` | 7 (3 guarded by `#else`, 3 unconditional static, 1 per-instance) |
| `[GeneratedRegex]` | 3 |
| `new Regex(` in instance constructor | 1 |
| `.Substring(` | 2 |
| Chained Regex.Replace | 1 (triple chain) |

---

## Findings

#### 1. Triple Regex.Replace Chain + .ToLower() in Underscore (1 instance) 🔴 Critical
**Impact:** 4 string allocations per call × millions of calls = massive GC pressure. `.ToLower()` is also culture-sensitive (potential correctness bug in Turkish locale).  
**Files:** CaseTransformExtensions.cs:L117-121  
**Fix:** Replace with a single-pass `string.Create()` or `StringBuilder` approach that walks the string once, inserting `_` at boundaries and lowercasing in-place. Use `ToLowerInvariant()`. On .NET 7+, convert `UnderscoreRegex1/2/3` to `[GeneratedRegex]`.

```csharp
// Suggested replacement for Underscore():
public static string Underscore(this string input)
{
    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(input)) return input;
    var sb = new StringBuilder(input.Length + 4);
    for (int i = 0; i < input.Length; i++)
    {
        char c = input[i];
        if (c == '-' || c == ' ')
        {
            sb.Append('_');
        }
        else if (char.IsUpper(c) && i > 0
            && (char.IsLower(input[i - 1])
                || (i + 1 < input.Length && char.IsUpper(input[i - 1]) && char.IsLower(input[i + 1]))))
        {
            sb.Append('_');
            sb.Append(char.ToLowerInvariant(c));
        }
        else
        {
            sb.Append(char.ToLowerInvariant(c));
        }
    }
    return sb.ToString();
}
```

#### 2. Per-Match Allocations in Pascalize (2 Substring + 1 ToUpper + 1 concat per match) 🔴 Critical
